      "content": "thanks for the term \"ghost inventory,\" that actually fits pretty well. but you mentioned a \"sneaky gremlin\" just now—was that just a figure of speech or are you suggesting there's something specific about the way these losses happen? i'm trying to figure out if this is something we can actually track with data, or if it's just one of those things that's impossible to pin down because it's so... well, sneaky.",
      "source": "evaluator"
